  "caseId": "case07",
  "description": "The WHEN YEARLYI arm at :239-255 with CONFIRMI = 'Y' - the second arm of the ordered EVALUATE, reached because MONTHLYI is spaces. No intrinsic is involved here: :243-246 move the current year and the literal '01' twice, and :250-251 move the literals '12' and '31', so the range is 1 January to 31 December of the current year and December's length is a literal rather than a computation. All seventeen records are pinned again with the year-range dates substituted, which is what proves the substitution points are per-request rather than baked into the template. Expected values are STATICALLY DERIVED by reading app/cbl/CORPT00C.cbl, its copybooks, app/bms/CORPT00.bms and app/csd/CARDDEMO.CSD - never captured from a COBOL run, which is impossible in this environment (risk R-A). Java has no transient data queue, so EXEC CICS WRITEQ TD QUEUE('JOBS') at :517 is reproduced through an explicit job-submission port; the eighty-byte content is identical and the dataset key JOBS names the TDQUEUE(JOBS) that app/csd/CARDDEMO.CSD:499-505 defines as RECORDSIZE(80) RECORDFORMAT(FIXED) BLOCKFORMAT(UNBLOCKED) DISPOSITION(MOD).",
